WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
From stray coffee cups in Westeros

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.080
to Bradley Cooper's fake baby,

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.570
things don't always go as planned

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.690
when filming a TV show or movie.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.730
There have been numerous
mistakes in the past decade

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:11.930
that slipped through the cracks

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:15.006
and made it onto the big and small screen.

00:00:15.006 --> 00:00:18.203
Here are 18 of the biggest
blunders of the 2010s.

00:00:20.144 --> 00:00:23.900
In 2019, HBO aired the final
season of "Game of Thrones,"

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.790
and while fans weren't exactly happy

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.670
with how everything turned
out with the rushed plot,

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.230
there was also a major gaffe

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.510
that managed to throw viewers
completely out of the fantasy.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.511
In this scene, a coffee
cup from craft services

00:00:36.511 --> 00:00:39.100
(no, it's technically not a Starbucks cup)

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.410
was accidentally left in the final cut.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.370
It's clearly visible on
the table next to Daenerys,

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.862
and, as far as we know,

00:00:45.862 --> 00:00:48.140
there were no baristas at Winterfell.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.190
The cup was later edited out of the shot.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.470
After the coffee-cup debacle,
no one would have expected

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:55.820
yet another mistake

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:58.370
in the final season of "Game of Thrones."

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.610
In one of the most important

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.240
and highly anticipated
scenes of the series,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.890
the leaders of Westeros were choosing

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.496
who would take the throne.

00:01:05.496 --> 00:01:07.737
Edmure Tully: I suppose
this is the most important

00:01:07.737 --> 00:01:09.645
moment of our lives.

00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:11.870
Narrator: Unfortunately,
someone on the cast or crew

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.520
left some water bottles
in a few of the shots,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.253
turning the serious moment
into a bit of a joke.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.350
There's a heartwarming
moment in "American Sniper"

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.163
that quickly turns laughable.

00:01:24.382 --> 00:01:27.160
In this scene, Bradley
Cooper has returned from war

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.710
and is picking up his child.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.380
But since director Clint Eastwood thought

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.140
using a real baby would
be too unpredictable,

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.080
they decided to use a doll instead.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.590
And it's painfully obvious,

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:39.910
especially when Cooper is seen

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.560
moving the baby's arm with his finger.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.450
The events in season
five of "Breaking Bad"

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.210
are set in 2009 and 2010,

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.120
but one of the characters

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.170
can apparently see into the future.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.040
In this scene, Todd's uncle references

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.767
the raid and death of Osama bin Laden.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:57.430
Jack Welker: Whacking bin
Laden wasn't this complicated.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.680
Narrator: Which didn't actually happen

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.395
until a year later, in 2011.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.460
In "The Dark Knight Rises,"

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.080
the sun seemingly sets super early.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.760
The stock market heist scene takes place

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.130
soon after the opening bell,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.830
and it's clearly light outside.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.020
But soon after, there's a car chase,

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.460
and when they all emerge from
the tunnel, it's pitch black.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.920
Dark "night" rises, indeed.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.870
But that wasn't the only
mistake in the film.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.940
Typos happen all the time,

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.930
but the copy editor at The Gotham Times

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.893
probably lost their job over this one.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.700
In the main headline on the front page,

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.033
heist is spelled wrong.

00:02:36.341 --> 00:02:38.050
In this scene, Rachel McAdams' character

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.870
is writing down notes
from her conversation

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:41.983
with one of the abuse victims at a diner.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.560
The camera cuts to the
notebook several times,

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.800
and while she seems to fill up the page,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.993
a few shots later it's nearly blank.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.293
Maybe it's disappearing ink?

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.360
During the final battle
scene in "The Avengers,"

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.620
there's a lot going on,

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.300
so it's not that surprising
that there would be

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.120
a few continuity errors here.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.570
In this scene, the front of a car

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.960
is clearly dented and beaten up,

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.810
but after Thor lands on the ground,

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.200
the car has miraculously
turned to perfect condition.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.620
A blessing from the gods.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:15.470
There's another continuity
error in the final battle.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:18.030
Here, we see Captain America
is shot in the stomach,

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.450
and his suit is torn and damaged.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:22.830
A few minutes later, however,

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.590
it's back to normal.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:28.630
Guess Captain America is also
a pretty good seamstress.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.290
Elsa belting out "Let it Go"

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.980
is one of the more memorable
scenes in "Frozen,"

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.940
but no matter how many
times you've watched it,

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.690
you may not have noticed this
one pretty bizarre error.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.658
In this scene, after
she lets down her hair,

00:03:40.658 --> 00:03:42.640
she swings around and her braid appears

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.203
to magically pass right through her arm.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:51.300
"Suicide Squad" wasn't exactly flawless,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.700
but there was one scene in the film

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.330
that makes absolutely no sense.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.410
In this scene, the characters

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.620
are all putting on their costumes,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.300
but Harley Quinn's transformation

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.500
is a bit more drastic than the others'.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.400
Somehow, she manages to get
a haircut and dye her hair

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.980
seconds after she puts on her outfit.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.883
Rick Flag: Seriously, what the
h---'s wrong with you people?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.100
Narrator: While technically
not in the show,

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.980
this promotional image for "Downton Abbey"

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.420
made headlines for something
fans spotted in the background.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:21.880
Can you find it?

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.680
Yes, like "Game of Thrones,"

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.150
there's a plastic water
bottle in the shot,

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:27.850
sitting right there on the mantle.

00:04:28.963 --> 00:04:30.330
You may have been too teary-eyed

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.200
at the sight of all
the Avengers assembling

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.313
to notice this one.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.050
In this scene, we clearly see Thanos

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.550
destroy Captain America's shield.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.908
It's cracked in half.

00:04:40.908 --> 00:04:41.883
But soon after,

00:04:41.883 --> 00:04:44.470
when the camera pans out
at the portals opening,

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.683
the shield is back to its original state.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.270
If only we could snap our fingers

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.993
and do the same for Iron Man.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.490
Henry Cavill is known as Superman,

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.440
but he appears to also have superpowers

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.314
in his role as agent August Walker

00:04:58.314 --> 00:05:00.730
in "Mission: Impossible - Fallout."

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.840
In this scene, Cavill's beard

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.840
quickly grows while he's punching.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.580
As if that wasn't bad enough,

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.793
a pocket also appears on his dress shirt.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.640
In the world of "The Walking Dead,"

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.430
physics apparently don't apply.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.270
In season five, Daryl and
Carol are trapped in a van

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.060
that's teetering on the
edge of an overpass.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.603
Eventually, the van
falls and flips forward,

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.203
but somehow, it lands on
its wheels seconds later.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.020
Before the coffee cup and water bottle,

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.810
there was another error
in "Game of Thrones"

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.240
that had people scratching their heads.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.160
In season six, we learned Melisandre

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.257
turns into an old woman when
she takes off her necklace,

00:05:43.257 --> 00:05:46.370
but in season four, there's a
scene with her in a bathtub,

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:50.243
sans necklace, and yet she's
still young and beautiful.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:55.310
While demogorgons and strange
young girls with telekinesis

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:57.050
aren't very realistic,

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.700
there's one mistake the production team

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.960
on "Stranger Things" made with the props.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.920
Throughout season one, the kids are using

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:06.200
realistic TRC-214 walkie-talkies

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.080
to communicate with each other.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:10.570
The only problem is that
these didn't actually exist

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.483
until about two years later, in 1985.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.410
While there's certainly
a lot of time-hopping

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.500
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.450
one jump in "Spider-Man: Homecoming"

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.990
seemed to mess everything up.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.210
The movie's supposed to be set

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:28.810
eight years after "The
Avengers," which was set in 2012,

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.880
hence "Homecoming" takes place in 2020,

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:34.260
but that doesn't line up
with the rest of the films,

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:38.010
like "Avengers: Infinity
War," which was set in 2018.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.340
So the entire timeline would get shifted,

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.200
making the dates the heroes jump back to

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.100
in "Endgame" incorrect.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.150
Director Joe Russo eventually admitted

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.200
that this "8 years later" title card

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.492
was "incorrect" during a press interview.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.580
Narrator: Were there
any other big mistakes

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.770
you noticed in the past decade?

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.103
Let us know in the comments.

